Mainline ends a request only from its interrupt and keeps the controller's own timeout off, so a
lost interrupt held the SDIO host forever: the aic8800 hung with ksdioirqd in mmc_wait_for_req_done.
Allwinner's driver ends such a request after 5 s, this one now too, and reports its registers.
D1 DMA segments stay at 4 KiB as in Allwinner's driver, a full 8 KiB one went out as size 0.
Controller errors print, the kernel has no dynamic debug.

